32.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134646432.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[BLOs to visit homes of missing pre-SIR voters, enrol via form 6]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/under-fire-ec-orders-special-drive-to-add-genuine-electors-left-out-during-sir/articleshow/134646432.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/under-fire-ec-orders-special-drive-to-add-genuine-electors-left-out-during-sir/articleshow/134646432.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-03T01:41:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Bharti Jain</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134646431,imgsize-255702.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Protests against CEC Gyanesh Kumar: Over 700 detained in Delhi, thousands attend CJP stir in Mumbai - top developments]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/protests-against-cec-gyanesh-kumar-over-700-detained-in-delhi-thousands-attend-cjp-stir-in-mumbai-top-developments/articleshow/134644594.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134644594.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Demonstrations are intensifying in Delhi and Mumbai, with protesters calling for Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar's resignation over perceived electoral roll issues. Approximately 700 individuals were detained in Delhi at Jantar Mantar. Meanwhile, thousands defied police orders to gather at Shivaji Park in Mumbai. Protests also spread to other cities, including Ahmedabad, Lucknow, and Patna, highlighting a growing movement.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/protests-against-cec-gyanesh-kumar-over-700-detained-in-delhi-thousands-attend-cjp-stir-in-mumbai-top-developments/articleshow/134644594.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/protests-against-cec-gyanesh-kumar-over-700-detained-in-delhi-thousands-attend-cjp-stir-in-mumbai-top-developments/articleshow/134644594.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T23:16:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134644747,imgsize-437800.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Lawyers’ body forms panel to review SIR: Ex-SC, HC judges to examine ‘constitutional &amp; statutory validity’]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sir-under-review-former-sc-hc-judges-to-examine-constitutional-statutory-validity-of-voter-roll-revision/articleshow/134644487.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134644487.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[A panel of five former judges is being formed to review the Election Commission's Special Intensive Revision. The Lawyers Association for Constitution emphasizes the panel's independence in assessing the review's validity and impact. Senior lawyers are expected to provide strategic legal advice to the panel throughout the process. The Election Commission has also initiated a drive to identify and re-enrol excluded eligible voters.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sir-under-review-former-sc-hc-judges-to-examine-constitutional-statutory-validity-of-voter-roll-revision/articleshow/134644487.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/sir-under-review-former-sc-hc-judges-to-examine-constitutional-statutory-validity-of-voter-roll-revision/articleshow/134644487.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T23:10:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134644587,imgsize-77530.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[BJP government made Haryana number one in drugs, corruption, crime: Hooda]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjp-government-made-haryana-number-one-in-drugs-corruption-crime-hooda/articleshow/134642744.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134642744.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[In a passionate speech at the Congress Block Workers' Conference in Tauru, Bhupinder Singh Hooda slammed the BJP government, claiming that under its leadership, Haryana has seen a grave decline in both development and safety. He highlighted the state's dismal performance in crime rates and economic growth, attributing this downturn to the BJP's neglect over the past 12 years.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjp-government-made-haryana-number-one-in-drugs-corruption-crime-hooda/articleshow/134642744.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/bjp-government-made-haryana-number-one-in-drugs-corruption-crime-hooda/articleshow/134642744.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T22:58:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Mahima Sharma</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134642753,imgsize-39616.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[India’s diversity, traditional knowledge can help build better world: RSS chief Mohan Bhagwat]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indias-diversity-traditional-knowledge-can-help-build-better-world-rss-chief-mohan-bhagwat/articleshow/134643992.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134643992.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[RSS chief Mohan Bhagwat highlighted Bharat's identity rooted in its languages, faiths, and cultures during a recent address. He emphasized the need for youth to be educated about Indian traditions while integrating global knowledge. Bhagwat referred to responses from an interfaith meeting, emphasizing universal truths shared by various philosophies. He encouraged passing on Bharat's identity and values to future generations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indias-diversity-traditional-knowledge-can-help-build-better-world-rss-chief-mohan-bhagwat/articleshow/134643992.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/indias-diversity-traditional-knowledge-can-help-build-better-world-rss-chief-mohan-bhagwat/articleshow/134643992.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T22:38:11+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134644107,imgsize-108580.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pargat Singh replaces Warring as Punjab Congress chief: Who he is and why Congress chose him]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pargat-singh-replaces-warring-as-punjab-congress-chief-who-he-is-and-why-congress-chose-him/articleshow/134643353.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134643353.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Pargat Singh has been chosen as the new president of the Punjab Pradesh Congress Committee. He replaces Amrinder Singh Raja Warring, who resigned amid party factional tensions. With the 2027 assembly elections approaching, Congress seeks to unify its internal divisions. Singh’s political experience as an MLA and former minister provides valuable legislative insights. His association with sports also aims to engage a younger voter base effectively.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pargat-singh-replaces-warring-as-punjab-congress-chief-who-he-is-and-why-congress-chose-him/articleshow/134643353.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/pargat-singh-replaces-warring-as-punjab-congress-chief-who-he-is-and-why-congress-chose-him/articleshow/134643353.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T22:00:06+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134643523,imgsize-72352.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Rahul Gandhi demands CEC Gyanesh Kumar’s resignation as protests erupt in Delhi, Mumbai]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rahul-gandhi-demands-cec-gyanesh-kumars-resignation-as-protests-erupt-in-delhi-mumbai/articleshow/134643388.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134643388.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Rahul Gandhi has called for Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar's resignation during ongoing protests. These protests arose over allegations of irregularities in the electoral-roll revision exercise. Approximately 700 protesters were detained in Delhi while trying to gather near Jantar Mantar for the demonstrations. Additional protests took place in Mumbai, where various groups demanded Kumar's resignation and accountability.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rahul-gandhi-demands-cec-gyanesh-kumars-resignation-as-protests-erupt-in-delhi-mumbai/articleshow/134643388.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/rahul-gandhi-demands-cec-gyanesh-kumars-resignation-as-protests-erupt-in-delhi-mumbai/articleshow/134643388.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-02T21:51:30+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpe